---
layout: null
---
[
{% for a in site.articles %}
  {
    "title": {{ a.title | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ a.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
    "category": {{ a.category | jsonify }},
    "categoryTitle": {{ site.help_categories | where: "id", a.category | first | map: "title" | first | jsonify }},
    "quick": {{ a.quick | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
    "tags": {{ a.tags | default: "" | jsonify }},
    "body": {{ a.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncate: 4000 | jsonify }},
    "draft": {{ a.needs_review | default: false }},
    "sections": [
      {%- comment -%}
        TA-569: one entry per H2 so a result can land on the section that
        answers the question, not the top of the article. kramdown gives every
        H2 an id (auto_ids); tools/check_anchors.py fails the build if one
        would not. Each piece after the split starts with the id.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign pieces = a.content | split: '<h2 id="' -%}
      {%- for piece in pieces offset: 1 -%}
        {%- assign id = piece | split: '"' | first -%}
        {%- assign head = piece | split: '</h2>' | first | split: '>' | last | strip_html | normalize_whitespace -%}
        {%- assign text = piece | split: '</h2>' | last | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncate: 600 -%}
        { "id": {{ id | jsonify }}, "title": {{ head | jsonify }}, "text": {{ text | jsonify }} }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{% endfor %}
]
